      "text": "79,735.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **135** and **591**, we'll follow a step-by-step multiplication process:\n\n1. **Multiply 135 by the ones place of 591 (which is 1):**\n   \n   \\[\n   135 \\times 1 = 135\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 135 by the tens place of 591 (which is 90):**\n   \n   \\[\n   135 \\times 90 = 12,\\!150\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 135 by the hundreds place of 591 (which is 500):**\n   \n   \\[\n   135 \\times 500 = 67,\\!500\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \n   \\[\n   135 + 12,\\!150 + 67,\\!500 = 79,\\!735\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{79,\\!735}\n\\]",
